# Per-repo functional-identifier allowlist.
#
# Widens what the listed paths may NAME. It does not widen what any file may
# CLAIM: the anchored attribution scan and the prose-credit scan still apply to
# every path below, so a co-author trailer, a Generated-By line, an Author:
# metadata key or a sentence asserting that a vendor authored this work is still
# refused here exactly as it is everywhere else. Verified by a negative control
# recorded in docs/evidence/ATTRIBUTION_CONTROL.md.
#
# Authorship remains Frank Asante Van Laarhoven alone.
#
# WHY THESE PATHS NEED VENDOR NAME STRINGS
#
# This repository's subject matter is a workbench whose default generation
# provider is a specific commercial model API, and whose pre-execution audit is
# REQUIRED to record the exact toolchain it ran under. The names below are
# therefore functional identifiers and recorded environment facts:
#
#   - the pre-execution audit records the CLI name and version, the model id,
#     and the list of connected tool servers. A precheck that omits the
#     toolchain it ran under is not an audit;
#   - the specification archive's literal filename contains a vendor name, and
#     the reconciliation record must name the file it could not find;
#   - a product requirement names the default model provider and the
#     administrator-approved alternative provider, because provider choice is
#     the governed decision being specified;
#   - the deviations log records that a provider interface exists but reports
#     NEEDS_CONFIGURATION because no credential is provisioned.
#
# Each is a statement about what the software talks to or ran on. None credits
# anybody. Narrowed to evidence records and the requirement matrix; source
# directories are deliberately not listed.

.attribution-allow
docs/evidence/*
docs/REQUIREMENTS.md
